## 1. Vendored fold inputs — from tt-bio

    examples/trpcage_no_msa.yaml
    examples/affinity_fkg.yaml
    examples/affinity_dhfr.yaml
    examples/affinity_tryp.yaml

    Source:   github.com/moritztng/tt-bio, examples/
    License:  MIT — Copyright (c) 2024 Jeremy Wohlwend, Gabriele Corso,
              Saro Passaro (tt-bio is built on the MIT-licensed Boltz-2 /
              Boltz-1 code and carries their copyright)

    Modifications: each file gains a header comment explaining why it is
    vendored here rather than read from a sibling checkout. The sequences and
    fold configuration are unchanged.

    Why vendored at all: this project previously pointed at
    ~/code/tt-boltz/examples/... — an absolute path into a repository it does
    not control. If that path moved, seven integration tests would have
    skipped silently while the suite still printed PASS, leaving the demo's
    headline mechanism untested. Copying the inputs makes their presence a
    fact about this repo.

## 2. Upstream contribution — derived from tt-bio

    docs/upstream/protenix-dump-fn/

    A patch adding a public `dump_fn` to `Protenix.fold`, which `OpenDDE.fold`
    already has. Contains diffs against tt-bio source.

    License:  MIT, as above. Offered back upstream; not a fork.

